Article 7 (Methods of Requesting Prohibition or Cessation)
Where an organization instituting a lawsuit requests a business entity to prohibit or cease an act infringing upon consumers' rights and interests under Article 74 (1) 3 of the Act, its written request shall state the following matters:
1. Name and address of the organization and name of its representative;
2. Contact information;
3. Name or trade name and address of the business entity;
4. A statement that the request is made under Article 74 (1) 3 of the Act;
5. Details of the infringing act and the conduct whose prohibition or cessation is sought.
